2. MG-Verilog  --  https://github.com/GATECH-EIC/MG-Verilog
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

What we redistribute from it: 68 derived supervised-fine-tuning rows --
44 rows in data/train.sample.jsonl and 24 rows in data/val.jsonl, each carrying
`meta.source == "mg-verilog"`. These are derived instruction/response pairs, not
raw upstream modules, but they are derived from MG-Verilog content.

It also redistributes data/rtlrepairdataset_train.jsonl: 5,775 repair pairs
whose seed modules come from MG-Verilog (per the Fairchild SFT mixture's dataset
card). Each row contains a mutated copy of an MG-Verilog module and the unified
diff that restores it.

