3. Resyn27k  --  https://github.com/hkust-zhiyao/RTL-Coder
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

NO ATTRIBUTION NOTICE IS REPRODUCED HERE BECAUSE THERE IS NO UPSTREAM LICENSE
TO REPRODUCE. This section is a disclosure, not a compliance claim.

`hkust-zhiyao/RTL-Coder` ships no LICENSE file. Verified 2026-08-16 by the
GitHub license API, which returns `"license": null` for the repository. With no
license grant, the default position is all rights reserved: redistribution of
`dataset/Resyn27k.json` or of derivatives of it is not affirmatively permitted
by any grant we can point to.

We nevertheless redistribute 12 derived supervised-fine-tuning rows -- 6 rows in
data/train.sample.jsonl and 6 rows in data/val.jsonl, each carrying
`meta.source == "resyn27k"`, and each containing a derived instruction and a
complete Verilog module. This was a deliberate decision, taken because the
corpus is load-bearing for a claim the paper makes: 18 of the 155 evaluation
specifications share a paraphrase of at least 12 consecutive words with a
Resyn27k *training* record, and dropping those 18 is the entire reason the
137-task clean subset exists. Removing the rows would leave the paper asserting
a decontamination result against a corpus the artifact never shows.

These 12 rows are NOT covered by the Apache-2.0 grant in LICENSE. They are
included for research inspection and reproducibility only. No reuse right over
them is granted or implied by this repository, and downstream users should treat
them as all-rights-reserved upstream material. Upstream additionally states that
the corpus was generated by GPT-3.5-turbo and that its authors adhere to
OpenAI's terms; those terms are not superseded here.

